+# Renderer Parity Tracker
+
+| Feature | CoopDX OpenGL ES behavior | Metal status | Evidence / remaining work |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Display-list and DynOS frontend | Shared `gfx_pc.c` interpreter and texture decoder | Must remain shared | No renderer port may bypass this frontend |
+| Color combiner | `ColorCombiner` command stream; generated GLSL | Not implemented yet | Build a full semantic MSL adapter; do not convert to the old packed ID |
+| Vertex stream | Clip-space position, UV0/1, optional fog/light map, combiner inputs | Not implemented yet | Derive `MTLVertexDescriptor` from combiner metadata |
+| Texture upload/cache | RGBA8 uploads; two tiles; N64 wrap/filter modes | Not implemented yet | Cache invalidation, sampler modes and repeated DynOS replacement tests |
+| Depth and decal | Backend depth test/write and z-mode decal callbacks | Not implemented yet | Pipeline/depth state parity tests |
+| Alpha/transparency | Alpha variant plus blend state and texture-edge discard | Not implemented yet | Correct blend factors/order and test translucent surfaces |
+| Fog | Per-vertex fog attribute under combiner flag | Not implemented yet | Preserve fog factor and color semantics |
+| Light-map path | Secondary UV, texture 1 and light-map color | Not implemented yet | Need audit the exact light-map uniform source |
+| Viewport/scissor | Callback-driven screen state | Not implemented yet | Drawable scale and orientation validation |
+| Frame lifecycle | SDL GL context, GL clear/swap | Not implemented yet | Metal drawable acquisition, command completion and present |
+| HUD/UI/DJUI | Same display-list frontend with blended draws | Not implemented yet | Validate text/texture paths after base material parity |
+| Character animation / DynOS | Same game and graphics frontend | Not implemented yet | Runtime-loaded geometry and texture invalidation test |
+| OpenGL ES fallback | Current iOS default | Preserved in source | Must remain known-good and recoverable from failed Metal initialization |
+
+Terms such as “Metal backend”, “iOS build”, and “parity” remain unverified until the corresponding compile/runtime/device evidence is recorded.
